# What ships to pub.dev. Anything a consumer of the package can't use is
# excluded here rather than in .gitignore, so it stays in the repo but out of
# the published archive.
#
# NOTE: .pubignore fully REPLACES .gitignore for publishing — when this file
# exists, pub stops consulting .gitignore, so every build/tooling path has to
# be repeated below.

# ── Build output and tool caches ──
build/
**/build/
.dart_tool/
**/.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
/coverage/

# ── Example app scaffolding ──
# The example is shipped for its `lib/` — that is what pub.dev renders and what
# pana scores. The generated per-platform host projects are ~6 MB of Gradle,
# Xcode and CMake boilerplate that no consumer builds from the archive; anyone
# who wants to run it clones the repo instead.
example/android/
example/ios/
example/web/
example/linux/
example/macos/
example/windows/
example/.gitignore
example/example.iml
example/pubspec.lock
example/test/

# ── Repo-internal tooling and docs ──
# docs/ is the GitHub Pages source for the example's remote-JSON endpoints
# (alaakhaledahmed.github.io/app_upgrade/version/*.json). It must stay in git so
# Pages keeps serving it, but shipping it would also trip pub's
# "rename docs/ to doc/" layout hint.
docs/
graphify-out/
CLAUDE.md
.github/

# ── Editor / OS noise ──
*.iml
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log
*.swp

# NOTE: screenshots/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the README embeds it with
# relative paths and pub.dev renders those on the package page.
# NOTE: test/ is deliberately NOT ignored — shipping tests is conventional and
# lets consumers verify the package they installed.
